This review concerns the export dated 4 October 2026. It is not a claim that the live desk has stopped receiving reports.

<Callout>The old “one issue, one fix” summary does not match the executable classification. Shared subjects and intake guesses are not sufficient evidence of a shared cause.</Callout>

## Count distinct reports, then resolve the tenant

<IncidentAudit />

## Separate the two problems

- **Parser:** the shared parser reads dates month-first for day-first tenants. Correct the interpretation of input; cover ambiguous dates and inspect the flagged one-day-move reports.
- **Hint:** booking-v3 tells users to type MM/DD/YYYY while interpreting dates day-first for these tenants. Align the guidance and accepted format. A parser fix alone does not establish that this mismatch was fixed.

Consult each report's tenant locale and form version, then its channel. Do not substitute browserLocale or intakeTag for that lookup.

## Queue timing is part of the evidence

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

Reports existed before they were merged into the large ticket. A later merge date does not make them new incidents. Use receivedAt for arrival and mergedAt for filing; do not conflate them.

## Triage and maintenance

- Keep separate tickets for the two classified problems; count unique IDs once and preserve their supporting records.
- Do not merge reports solely because their subject strings match. Compare behavior and the relevant tenant/form context; leave unsupported causes unresolved.
- The accepted dedupe decision is historical. Propose a new decision instead of editing the old accepted record in place.
- Recheck the live queue before submitting final counts. Tables here are computed from the current bundled export, not hard-coded into prose.

